s9_015_numbers_s11.py = s9_015_numbers.py for S11 (option C; TESTS.md addendum 16) -> paper/numbers/bf_template_metrics_s9_015_s11.json.
The bf_template_metrics numbers for the step-9 blockface template on the 0.15 mm grid (TESTS.md addenda 13 and 16; option C, S11),
from its saved products only, beside the 2b record (bf_template_metrics_d2b.json, d2bs8 at 0.25 mm, unchanged):
  members: S11 = 11 brains (S12 without MR263), 22 blockface inputs (each brain and its mirror), no b0-only member;
  brain = the template's brainmask (P >= 0.5); photographed = brain & photo_share >= 0.5 (the real mask);
  synthesized (the paper's "predicted") = brain & photo_share < 0.5, the same rule as d2bs8's synth_mask; also brain & photo_share = 0;
  symmetry: max |V - mirror(V)| of grey, rgb, brainmask, real mask (exact 0 expected);
  the same in the MRI template's frame (out_015_s11/in_mri_template, through d2bs8_s5sym, 0.25 mm), for information.
    python step9/s9_015_numbers_s11.py  -> paper/numbers/bf_template_metrics_s9_015_s11.json
